{#- One home for the board's octopus, because the page renders it on load and the pushed board replaces it, so the first review takes the first-day panel away and an idle board gets the asleep octopus without a reload. The waiting octopus sits above the panel's words (DESIGN.md, First day). The steps name only what this install does: the head's Set up Intakt (`_board_setup.html.twig`, pushed with this panel) stays the one setup action (#2067, D3). -#}
{%- set pose = board.mascot -%}
{%- set idle = board.idleProjects -%}
{%- if board.firstDay -%}
<section class="firstday" id="board-octopus" aria-labelledby="board-octopus-h">
    {{- include('dashboard/components/character.html.twig', {character: pose, size: 144}, with_context = false) -}}
    <div>
        <h2 id="board-octopus-h">Give Intakt its first task</h2>
        <ol>
            <li>Choose <strong>Set up Intakt</strong> and add an AI provider and a project.</li>
            <li>Start the first review there. It shows up in In review while the panel reviews the change, then in Done once the judge decides.</li>
            <li>Reviewers show up on the Status page while they review it.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>
{%- elseif pose is not null -%}
{#- Decoration only, on the empty board with nothing running, because the empty-column lines already say what lands where (2026-11-14 mascot decision; #2732). -#}
<div class="asleep" id="board-octopus">{{ include('dashboard/components/character.html.twig', {character: pose, size: 144}, with_context = false) }}</div>
{%- elseif idle is not empty -%}
{#- Some projects are at rest while another works, so the asleep octopus waits hidden and assets/board-octopus.js shows it while the project filter shows one of them (#2732). -#}
<div class="asleep" id="board-octopus" data-idle-projects="{{ idle|json_encode }}" hidden>{{ include('dashboard/components/character.html.twig', {character: enum('Intakt\\Core\\Dashboard\\Domain\\MascotPose').Asleep, size: 144}, with_context = false) }}</div>
{%- else -%}
{#- An empty hidden target stays, so a board that becomes empty again gets its octopus back on the next push (#2437). -#}
<span id="board-octopus" hidden></span>
{%- endif -%}
